# DentCast Cursor router

> **Publish-queue check — first, before anything else.** If the request mentions the publish queue («صف انتشار», branch `queue` of this repo), then: to **publish** from it («از صف انتشار منتشر کن», «قدیمی‌ترین مقالهٔ صف رو منتشر کن», «یه مقاله تو صف انتشار دارم» with no article or paper attached), read only `.dentcast/workflows/queue-route.md` and follow it (publish day runs on GitHub Actions: dispatch `.github/workflows/queue-publish.yml` and monitor it, never push or upload publication files from the agent sandbox; a fresh session runs `python3 tools/queue_publish.py status` first; two deliveries; the agent merges as soon as every gate is green, without asking (founder 2026-11-07); nothing else is read or done); to **report** the queue's status («صف انتشار چی داره؟»), read only `.dentcast/workflows/publish-queue.md`; to **prepare** an item («بذارش تو صف انتشار», «برای صف انتشار آماده‌اش کن», an article or paper attached), read `.dentcast/workflows/publish-queue.md` completely and then, once and completely, the queue-prep reading pack it names (`tools/dentcast_publish_readpack.py --queue-prep`, which assembles its «فهرست خواندن» byte for byte: module 01, module 02, module 06 Part 1 with a paper, module 08 and the listed sections of 03, 04, 05, 07, 10, 11, 12 and `en-version.md`). Queue work reads no global sections (the «Before content changes» rule below is for site files); `agent-parity.md` applies to it only through its «توانمندی ندارم» protocol. Otherwise ignore this note.

**LIVE_MODULAR_PUBLISHING_ENABLED.** There is exactly one live route per task — the table below — and no legacy, staging or draft copy of these instructions exists in the tree. An older version lives only in Git history and is never execution authority.

Before content changes, read `.dentcast/workflows/global/README.md`, the complete active sections selected by that router for the current edit scope, and `.dentcast/workflows/agent-parity.md`. All clients use these same rules. Exception: publishing an item from the queue reads only `.dentcast/workflows/queue-route.md`; its tools carry these rules.

New publication → `.dentcast/workflows/README.md`. Read complete `modules/01-hard-rules.md` and `02-routing-intake.md`, then all applicable verbatim rules in the ledger order of `publish-checkpoints.md`: full modules by default, or the verified readpack (README). No AI summaries or unverified omissions. Agent proposals are built and reported, not asked; the founder gets at most three messages (M1 open facts, M3b still-flagged Part 3b sentences, M2 exam questions) plus real decisions. Preserve source-dependent DES/Fidelity, category exceptions, English and final Phase F.

After a new v2 publication's second delivery is confirmed, immediately tell the user that the agent-side work has reached Push 2, GitHub Actions is running the remaining mechanical delivery (C.8 onward, delivery 3, and the PR when the `QUEUE_PUBLISH_TOKEN` secret is configured, otherwise the agent opens it by hand), and the agent is monitoring it. Include the branch, Push-2 SHA and Actions run link when available. Do not go silent or call the publication complete. Keep checking the run until it succeeds or fails, without periodic status messages: then merge as soon as every gate is green, without asking, and report once at the merge (`.dentcast/workflows/publish-after-push2.md`).

**Interrupted publication** («انتشار ناقص داشتم»), the run state `.dentcast/PUBLISH-HANDOFF.md` and recovery through `.dentcast/workflows/publish-handoff.md`: `.dentcast/workflows/publish-checkpoints.md`, «Interrupted publication».

## Routes

| Request | Active workflow |
|---|---|
| New content or attached paper (with or without text) | `.dentcast/workflows/README.md` |
| Existing-page English | `.dentcast/workflows/en-version.md` |
| Ads | `.dentcast/workflows/ads.md` |
| Ad statistics | `.dentcast/workflows/spot-report.md` |
| Glossary authoring | `.claude/skills/glossary-writer/SKILL.md` (same file as `.agents/skills/glossary-writer/SKILL.md`) |
| Cross-linking | `.dentcast/workflows/cross-link.md` |
| New section | `.dentcast/workflows/new-section.md` |
| Offline publishing | `.dentcast/offline-publish.md` |
| Minimal publications from /admin (setup, import into git, completion) | `.dentcast/quick-publish.md` |
| External Fidelity | `.dentcast/workflows/external-fidelity.md` |
| Publish queue on branch `queue` (prepare, status) | `.dentcast/workflows/publish-queue.md` |
| Publish an item from the queue (publish day) | `.dentcast/workflows/queue-route.md` (only this) |

Detailed triggers and specialty conditions: `.dentcast/workflows/routing-details.md`. Read the selected specialty workflow completely. New content uses the modular sequence, including paper-only and category exceptions.

Update AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and Cursor routing together when shared routes change. Never store private inputs in public Git history.

## Per-step checkpoints and delivery batches

Ledger, the save point (once C.4.13 starts), Push 2 (after `C.6`), delivery 3 by `post-cut2-mechanical.yml`, text lock, paper-only and completion: `.dentcast/workflows/publish-checkpoints.md`.
